  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Twibikeko Cooperative Society Cooking oil Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Twibikeko Cooperative has 435 members including 232 male and 203 female. The cooperative facilitates members as well as non-members to produce maize and groundnuts. Twibikeko cooperative wishes to engage in processing and marketing of cooking oil from groundnuts produced in the area. The cooking oil will be sold to the community and surrounding locations. The cooperative will also process groundnuts at a fee for the farmers and the farmers will retain the by-product (stock feed) that they can sell or feed their animals.</narrative>
  </description>
